:: reading.paint.start.morning
{=

Sun-light warms ($funcReveal: "the makeshift curtain,", "veil") (either:
    [sparkling diamond-sands on a supple beach,],
    [gold and amber and red and red and red,],
    [gentle echoes of that which roars in the heavens,],
)
` `which you find yourself hesitant to touch, let alone disturb.

|veil)[
<br>
Behind this illuminated veil is the unfinished painting - a pale imitation of the splendor that is presently plain to your eyes. If only you could ($funcReveal: "steal this light,", "stolen") then you would accept any Promethean punishment.]

|stolen)[
<br>
Alas, stolen, you have not. Your own ability has thus far fallen short. ($funcReveal: "How cruel", "mockery") it would be to expose the malformed fetus to its superior.]

|mockery)[
<br>
It would be a mockery for both you and your subject.
(t8n: "dissolve")(show: ?notRightNow)
]

|notRightNow)[
<br>
No, not right now. Your muse, ever Sun-shy, is in hiding, so you tell yourself.
(t8n: "dissolve")(show: ?mainDone)
]

:: done.paint.start.morning
{=

